==Notes==
*Link Redirection can be equipped on [[Kubrow]]s, [[Kavat]]s, [[MOA (Companion)|MOAs]], and [[Hound (Companion)|Hounds]], but '''not''' on [[Sentinels]].
*Link Redirection cannot be equipped simultaneously with {{M|Calculated Redirection}}.
*{{M|Redirection}}, {{M|Primed Vigor}}, and {{M|Augur Accord}} can help drastically improve a Beast's maximum shields, as this mod uses the player's maximum shields as the base.
*Link Redirection will allow most direct forms of shield recovery to apply to the pet, including {{WF|Harrow}}'s {{A|Condemn}}, {{WF|Hildryn}}'s {{A|Pillage}}, the {{Weapon|Rakta Dark Dagger}}'s passive, {{WF|Volt}}'s {{M|Capacitance}}, and {{WF|Protea}}'s {{A|Grenade Fan}}.
**Link Redirection does '''not''' create overshields.
**Link Redirection does not share passive shield regeneration effects such as {{Arcane|Arcane Aegis}}.
**Link Redirection does not apply shield generation or overshields from the [[Augur Set]] or {{M|Brief Respite}}.
*With a fully ranked copy of Link Redirection, the Warframe's minimal required shield value to activate {{M|Reinforced Bond}}'s fire rate bonus depends on the base shield value of the equipped companion:
**{{Companion|Adarza Kavat}} and {{Companion|Smeeta Kavat}} have the lowest base shield value of 230. The equipped Warframe needs at least 776 shields.
**A [[Hound (Companion)|Hound]] with [[Core (Component)#Adlet|Adlet]] and [[Bracket#Cela|Cela]] has the highest base shield value of 585. The equipped Warframe needs at least 492 shields.
**{{WF|Khora}} needs at least 960 shields, as {{Companion|Venari}} does not have any base shields, but can still equip Link Redirection to gain shields.

==Trivia==
*Prior to {{ver|34}}, this mod was named '''Link Shields'''.

